openfont.library/--background--                 openfont.library/--background--

   PURPOSE
	openfont.library is the Open stack's font service for AmigaOS 3.2 on
	the 68040: finding a font, shaping text with OpenType's rules, its
	metrics, and each glyph's pixels. Programs call it in place of
	FreeType, HarfBuzz and fontconfig. It reads, shapes and draws fonts
	with its own code.

	It is built for the 68040 with its FPU, and refuses to open unless
	exec reports both (AFF_68040 and AFF_FPU40): not on an LC040.

   VERSION 1 IS A PREVIEW
	Its calls and structures may still change. They are frozen from
	version 2, once OpenFont's design tests pass. Open version 1
	exactly if you depend on its layout.

   TEXT
	Text is UTF-8, with its length in bytes; OF_ShapeA (revision 3)
	also takes UTF-16. Positions, advances and metrics are 26.6 fixed
	point pixels: 64 is one pixel.

   FACES
	A face is one font of a file (a collection, .ttc or .otc, holds
	several). Open one by path (OF_OpenFaceA) or by family
	(OF_FindFaceA). A face has a pixel size, 16 when it opens.

	A face may fall back to up to eight others (OF_AddFallback): where
	it has no glyph for a cluster of the text, the next face in its
	chain shapes that cluster. Each shaped glyph says which face it
	came from (OFGlyph.gl_Face), and OF_GetFallback gives that face, to
	draw the glyph with.

	Faces are counted: a face added as a fallback is held by the face
	it serves, and is freed when its last holder closes it.

   THE FONT INDEX
	OF_FindFaceA looks in FONTS:, LIBS:WebBrowser/Fonts, the folders
	listed one a line in ENVARC:OpenFont/FontDirs, and any a program
	adds with OF_AddFontDir. It knows each face's family, style, weight,
	width and slant, kept in ENVARC:OpenFont/FontIndex, which it brings
	up to date when a folder's date says something in it changed.

	ENVARC:OpenFont/Aliases holds the user's own aliases, one a line:
	    Name=Family,Family
	OpenFont's own follow them: sans-serif, serif and monospace;
	Arial, Helvetica, Times New Roman, Times, Courier New and Courier
	(to the Liberation fonts, which keep their metrics); and others.
	ENVARC:OpenFont/Fallbacks is the default fallback chain, families
	separated by commas.

   FILES AND TASKS
	Calls that read files (opening a face or a cache, finding a face,
	adding a font folder, rescanning) must come from a process. From a
	plain task they fail with OFERR_NOTPROCESS. The other calls may come
	from any task.

   STACK
	Every call does its work on the library's own stack, so callers need
	no more than their usual. Calls from several tasks are taken one at
	a time.

   PATCHES
	openfont.library patches nothing in the system.

openfont.library/OF_AddFallback                 openfont.library/OF_AddFallback

   NAME
	OF_AddFallback -- add a face to another's fallback chain (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_AddFallback(face, fallback)
	D0                     A0    A1

	LONG OF_AddFallback(struct OFFace *, struct OFFace *);

   FUNCTION
	Adds fallback to the end of face's chain, and holds it: the caller
	may close its own handle on fallback afterwards.

   RESULT
	error - OFERR_OK; OFERR_RANGE when the chain holds OF_MAX_FALLBACKS
	        already; OFERR_ARGUMENT for a face falling back to itself,
	        or to a face whose fallbacks (or theirs, however far) lead
	        back to it: such a loop would keep its faces open.

   SEE ALSO
	OF_GetFallback(), OF_ShapeText()

openfont.library/OF_AddFontDir                   openfont.library/OF_AddFontDir

   NAME
	OF_AddFontDir -- look for fonts in one more folder (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_AddFontDir(dir)
	D0                    A0

	LONG OF_AddFontDir(CONST_STRPTR);

   FUNCTION
	Adds dir to the folders OF_FindFaceA looks in, until the library is
	expunged. It is indexed the next time a face is found. To add a
	folder for every program, list it in ENVARC:OpenFont/FontDirs.

	Must be called from a process: the first call that needs the index
	reads its settings from ENVARC:OpenFont.

   RESULT
	error - OFERR_OK (also when dir is listed already); OFERR_RANGE
	        when the library knows sixteen folders, its own and
	        FontDirs' included; OFERR_NOTPROCESS.

openfont.library/OF_CacheGetGlyph             openfont.library/OF_CacheGetGlyph

   NAME
	OF_CacheGetGlyph -- a glyph from a compiled cache (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_CacheGetGlyph(cache, pixels, codepoint, bitmap, glyph)
	D0                       A0     D0      D1         A1      A2

	LONG OF_CacheGetGlyph(struct OFCache *, ULONG, ULONG,
	                      struct OFBitmap *, ULONG *);

   FUNCTION
	Fills bitmap with the codepoint's glyph at pixels, from the cache:
	no font is read and nothing is rasterised. glyph, when not NULL,
	receives its glyph number. Free the bitmap with OF_FreeBitmap.

   RESULT
	error - OFERR_OK; OFERR_RANGE when the cache has no such size or
	        codepoint.

openfont.library/OF_CacheMatchesFace       openfont.library/OF_CacheMatchesFace

   NAME
	OF_CacheMatchesFace -- was this cache compiled from this face (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	match = OF_CacheMatchesFace(cache, face)
	D0                          A0     A1

	LONG OF_CacheMatchesFace(struct OFCache *, struct OFFace *);

   FUNCTION
	Compares the fingerprint the cache was compiled with to the face's
	own, so a cache of an older font is never used for a newer one. The
	first call for a face hashes its whole font, which is already in
	memory, once.

   RESULT
	match - TRUE or FALSE.

openfont.library/OF_CharIndex                     openfont.library/OF_CharIndex

   NAME
	OF_CharIndex -- the glyph a codepoint maps to (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	glyph = OF_CharIndex(face, codepoint)
	D0                   A0    D0

	ULONG OF_CharIndex(struct OFFace *, ULONG);

   RESULT
	glyph - in this face alone, not its fallbacks; 0 when it has none.

openfont.library/OF_CloseCache                   openfont.library/OF_CloseCache

   NAME
	OF_CloseCache -- close a compiled cache (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	OF_CloseCache(cache)
	              A0

	VOID OF_CloseCache(struct OFCache *);

openfont.library/OF_CloseFace                     openfont.library/OF_CloseFace

   NAME
	OF_CloseFace -- let go of a face (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	OF_CloseFace(face)
	             A0

	VOID OF_CloseFace(struct OFFace *);

   FUNCTION
	The face is freed when its last holder lets go of it: the program
	that opened it, and any face it is a fallback of. NULL is ignored.

openfont.library/OF_ErrorString                 openfont.library/OF_ErrorString

   NAME
	OF_ErrorString -- what an error code means (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	text = OF_ErrorString(error)
	D0                    D0

	CONST_STRPTR OF_ErrorString(LONG);

   RESULT
	text - in English, never NULL.

openfont.library/OF_FindFaceA                     openfont.library/OF_FindFaceA

   NAME
	OF_FindFaceA -- open the best face for a family (V1)
	OF_FindFace -- varargs stub for OF_FindFaceA

   SYNOPSIS
	face = OF_FindFaceA(family, tags)
	D0                  A0      A1

	struct OFFace *OF_FindFaceA(CONST_STRPTR, CONST struct TagItem *);

	face = OF_FindFace(family, tag1, ...)

   FUNCTION
	Opens the face of the installed fonts that best matches family,
	weight and slant: the family itself, then the user's aliases, then
	OpenFont's own, then the generic family sans-serif. The default
	fallback chain is added unless OFA_Fallbacks is FALSE. With
	OFA_Exact TRUE (revision 3) it stops after the aliases and returns
	NULL when neither the family nor an alias of it is installed, for
	programs with their own list of families to try, such as a browser
	with CSS font-family. Brings the font index up to date first if a
	folder has changed.

	Must be called from a process.

   INPUTS
	family - a family name ("DejaVu Sans"), an alias ("Arial") or a
	         generic family ("sans-serif", "serif", "monospace"). NULL
	         means sans-serif.
	tags - OFA_Weight (ULONG, 400), OFA_Italic (BOOL, FALSE),
	       OFA_Size (ULONG, 16; 0 keeps the face's own),
	       OFA_Fallbacks (BOOL, TRUE), OFA_Exact (BOOL, FALSE),
	       OFA_Error (LONG *): OFERR_FONT when no font is installed,
	       or why the face chosen did not open (as OF_OpenFaceA).

   RESULT
	face - or NULL.

openfont.library/OF_FindFaceForCharA       openfont.library/OF_FindFaceForCharA

   NAME
	OF_FindFaceForCharA -- a face that has a character (V1, revision 3)
	OF_FindFaceForChar -- varargs stub

   SYNOPSIS
	face = OF_FindFaceForCharA(codepoint, tags)
	D0                         D0         A0

	struct OFFace *OF_FindFaceForCharA(ULONG, const struct TagItem *);
	struct OFFace *OF_FindFaceForChar(ULONG, Tag, ...);

   FUNCTION
	Opens a face with a glyph for codepoint: the default fallback
	chain's families first (ENVARC:OpenFont/Fallbacks), then each
	family's best face for the weight and slant, in the index's order.
	The face has no fallbacks of its own. A layout engine calls it for
	text its fonts have no glyphs for, and keeps what it gets. It reads
	files: a process only.

   INPUTS
	tags - OFA_Weight, OFA_Italic, OFA_Size (16), OFA_Error.

   RESULT
	face - or NULL: none has it (OFERR_FONT), or OFERR_NOTPROCESS.

openfont.library/OF_FreeBitmap                   openfont.library/OF_FreeBitmap

   NAME
	OF_FreeBitmap -- free a glyph's pixels (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	OF_FreeBitmap(bitmap)
	              A0

	VOID OF_FreeBitmap(struct OFBitmap *);

   FUNCTION
	Frees bm_Pixels from OF_RasterGlyph or OF_CacheGetGlyph and clears
	the structure. The structure itself is the caller's.

openfont.library/OF_GetFaceInfo                 openfont.library/OF_GetFaceInfo

   NAME
	OF_GetFaceInfo -- a face's names and metrics (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_GetFaceInfo(face, info)
	D0                     A0    A1

	LONG OF_GetFaceInfo(struct OFFace *, struct OFFaceInfo *);

   FUNCTION
	Fills info: family and style, weight and width, flags (italic,
	fixed width, scalable, colour), units per em, the glyph count, how
	many faces its file holds, and the ascender, descender and line
	height at the face's current pixel size.

openfont.library/OF_GetFaceMetrics           openfont.library/OF_GetFaceMetrics

   NAME
	OF_GetFaceMetrics -- a face's measurements (V1, revision 3)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_GetFaceMetrics(face, metrics)
	D0                        A0    A1

	LONG OF_GetFaceMetrics(struct OFFace *, struct OFFaceMetrics *);

   FUNCTION
	Fills metrics at the face's pixel size, in 26.6 pixels with y up:
	the line's ascender, descender and gap (as OFFaceInfo's), the x and
	capital heights (OS/2, or measured from 'x' and 'H'), the underline
	and strikeout (post and OS/2), the widest advance and the space's.

   RESULT
	error - 0, or OFERR_ARGUMENT.

openfont.library/OF_GetFallback                 openfont.library/OF_GetFallback

   NAME
	OF_GetFallback -- one face of a fallback chain (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	f = OF_GetFallback(face, n)
	D0                 A0    D0

	struct OFFace *OF_GetFallback(struct OFFace *, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	n 0 is face itself; 1 to the chain's length, its fallbacks in
	order. Use it with OFGlyph.gl_Face to draw a shaped glyph. A
	fallback is set to face's pixel size as it is returned (one face may
	be a fallback of several), so call this for each glyph you draw
	rather than keeping the result. The face returned is not held for
	the caller: do not close it.

   RESULT
	f - or NULL past the end of the chain.

openfont.library/OF_GetFontTable               openfont.library/OF_GetFontTable

   NAME
	OF_GetFontTable -- one of a face's tables (V1, revision 3)

   SYNOPSIS
	table = OF_GetFontTable(face, tag, length)
	D0                      A0    D0   A1

	CONST_APTR OF_GetFontTable(struct OFFace *, ULONG, ULONG *);

   FUNCTION
	The table tag ('MATH', 'OS/2', 'GSUB') as it is in the font file,
	or NULL when the face has none. *length (when length is not NULL)
	is its size in bytes. It lives as long as the face: don't change
	or free it.

openfont.library/OF_GlyphAdvance               openfont.library/OF_GlyphAdvance

   NAME
	OF_GlyphAdvance -- a glyph's advance in font units (V1, revision 1)

   SYNOPSIS
	advance = OF_GlyphAdvance(face, glyph)
	D0                        A0    D0

	LONG OF_GlyphAdvance(struct OFFace *, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	The glyph's horizontal advance as the font gives it (hmtx), in
	font units: OFFaceInfo's fi_UnitsPerEm to the em. Not scaled, not
	shaped.

   RESULT
	advance - or -1 for a glyph the face doesn't have.

openfont.library/OF_GlyphAdvancePx           openfont.library/OF_GlyphAdvancePx

   NAME
	OF_GlyphAdvancePx -- a glyph's advance at the face's size (V1, revision 3)

   SYNOPSIS
	advance = OF_GlyphAdvancePx(face, glyph)
	D0                          A0    D0

	LONG OF_GlyphAdvancePx(struct OFFace *, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	The glyph's horizontal advance at the face's pixel size, in 26.6
	pixels, unrounded, as shaping gives it before kerning. -1 for a
	glyph the face doesn't have.

openfont.library/OF_GlyphExtents               openfont.library/OF_GlyphExtents

   NAME
	OF_GlyphExtents -- a glyph's ink box (V1, revision 3)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_GlyphExtents(face, glyph, extents)
	D0                      A0    D0     A1

	LONG OF_GlyphExtents(struct OFFace *, ULONG, struct OFGlyphExtents *);

   FUNCTION
	The box of the glyph's outline points at the face's size, in 26.6
	pixels with y up: from the pen to its left edge, from the baseline
	up to its top, its width and its height. All 0 for a space. A face
	with no outlines gives its bitmap's box.

   RESULT
	error - 0, or OFERR_RANGE (no such glyph), OFERR_FONT,
	        OFERR_MEMORY.

openfont.library/OF_GlyphOutline               openfont.library/OF_GlyphOutline

   NAME
	OF_GlyphOutline -- a glyph's outline (V1, revision 3)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_GlyphOutline(face, glyph, outline)
	D0                      A0    D0     A1

	LONG OF_GlyphOutline(struct OFFace *, ULONG, struct OFOutline *);

   FUNCTION
	The glyph's outline at the face's size as verbs and points, 26.6
	pixels with y up, for a program that draws or clips with paths
	(WebCore's text as paths, SVG, canvas). OFPV_MOVE and OFPV_LINE
	take one point, OFPV_QUAD two (control, end), OFPV_CUBIC three,
	OFPV_CLOSE none. Each contour begins with a move and ends with a
	close. TrueType's implied on-curve points are made explicit.

	The library fills ol_Verbs and ol_Points up to ol_MaxVerbs and
	ol_MaxPoints (a point is two LONGs) and always sets ol_NumVerbs and
	ol_NumPoints to the whole outline's, so a call with no buffers
	measures.

   RESULT
	error - 0, OFERR_BUFFER when it did not all fit, OFERR_RANGE (no
	        such glyph), OFERR_FONT, OFERR_MEMORY.

openfont.library/OF_MeasureText                 openfont.library/OF_MeasureText

   NAME
	OF_MeasureText -- the advance of a shaped run (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	advance = OF_MeasureText(face, utf8, bytes)
	D0                       A0    A1    D0

	LONG OF_MeasureText(struct OFFace *, CONST_STRPTR, ULONG);

   RESULT
	advance - the sum of the run's advances, 26.6, its fallbacks
	          included. 0 on failure.

openfont.library/OF_OpenCache                     openfont.library/OF_OpenCache

   NAME
	OF_OpenCache -- open a compiled glyph cache (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	cache = OF_OpenCache(path)
	D0                   A0

	struct OFCache *OF_OpenCache(CONST_STRPTR);

   FUNCTION
	Reads a cache that openfontcompile made: a font's glyphs, compiled
	once at the sizes a program uses most. Must be called from a
	process.

openfont.library/OF_OpenFaceA                     openfont.library/OF_OpenFaceA

   NAME
	OF_OpenFaceA -- open a face from a font file (V1)
	OF_OpenFace -- varargs stub for OF_OpenFaceA

   SYNOPSIS
	face = OF_OpenFaceA(path, tags)
	D0                  A0    A1

	struct OFFace *OF_OpenFaceA(CONST_STRPTR, CONST struct TagItem *);

	face = OF_OpenFace(path, tag1, ...)

   FUNCTION
	Reads a TrueType or OpenType font (.ttf, .otf, .ttc, .otc) into
	memory and opens one of its faces. Must be called from a process.

   INPUTS
	path - the font file.
	tags - OFA_Index (ULONG, 0): the face of a collection;
	       OFA_Size (ULONG, 16): the pixel size to start at;
	       OFA_Error (LONG *): why it failed: OFERR_IO (the file),
	       OFERR_MEMORY, OFERR_FONT (not a font it reads),
	       OFERR_NOTPROCESS.

   RESULT
	face - or NULL.

openfont.library/OF_OpenFaceMemoryA         openfont.library/OF_OpenFaceMemoryA

   NAME
	OF_OpenFaceMemoryA -- a face from a font in memory (V1, revision 3)
	OF_OpenFaceMemory -- varargs stub

   SYNOPSIS
	face = OF_OpenFaceMemoryA(data, size, tags)
	D0                        A0    D0    A1

	struct OFFace *OF_OpenFaceMemoryA(CONST_APTR, ULONG, const struct TagItem *);
	struct OFFace *OF_OpenFaceMemory(CONST_APTR, ULONG, Tag, ...);

   FUNCTION
	Opens a face from size bytes of a TrueType or OpenType font (or a
	collection) at data, as a web font arrives. The face keeps its own
	copy, so data may be freed at once. Any task may call it.

   INPUTS
	tags - OFA_Index, OFA_Size (16), OFA_Error.

   RESULT
	face - or NULL: OFERR_FONT (not a font it reads), OFERR_MEMORY,
	       OFERR_ARGUMENT.

openfont.library/OF_OpenTextFont               openfont.library/OF_OpenTextFont

   NAME
	OF_OpenTextFont -- an Amiga font as a TextFont (V1, revision 2)

   SYNOPSIS
	font = OF_OpenTextFont(textAttr)
	D0                     A0

	struct TextFont *OF_OpenTextFont(CONST struct TextAttr *);

   FUNCTION
	What diskfont.library's OpenDiskFont does, without diskfont.library
	or bullet.library: the font named in textAttr (a TTextAttr too),
	from memory or from FONTS: (or the name's own directory when it has
	a path), matched, and scaled to the size asked for unless
	FPF_DESIGNED is set. An outline font (an .otag beside its .font) is
	drawn at the size by openfont.library itself, characters 32 to 255,
	at the TTextAttr's TA_DeviceDPI, else 72 dpi. A font loaded here
	joins the system's font list, as OpenDiskFont's do, so graphics'
	OpenFont finds it next time.

	Only a process can call it (it reads files).

   RESULT
	font - the TextFont, to be closed with graphics.library's CloseFont,
	or NULL when there is none (or the caller is not a process).

   NOTES
	Programs that used OpenDiskFont call this instead: open
	openfont.library version 1 and check lib_Revision is 2 or more.
	Fonts nobody has open are freed when the library is expunged; the
	library stays while one of its fonts is in use.

openfont.library/OF_RasterGlyph                 openfont.library/OF_RasterGlyph

   NAME
	OF_RasterGlyph -- a glyph's 8-bit coverage (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_RasterGlyph(face, glyph, bitmap)
	D0                     A0    D0     A1

	LONG OF_RasterGlyph(struct OFFace *, ULONG, struct OFBitmap *);

   FUNCTION
	Draws glyph at the face's pixel size, antialiased, one byte a pixel
	(0 clear, 255 solid), into a buffer the library allocates. Free it
	with OF_FreeBitmap. An empty glyph (a space) gives a 0 by 0 bitmap
	with bm_Pixels NULL, and its advance.

openfont.library/OF_RasterGlyphMatrix     openfont.library/OF_RasterGlyphMatrix

   NAME
	OF_RasterGlyphMatrix -- a glyph's coverage through a matrix (V1, revision 1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_RasterGlyphMatrix(face, glyph, matrix, bitmap)
	D0                           A0    D0     A1      A2

	LONG OF_RasterGlyphMatrix(struct OFFace *, ULONG, const LONG *,
	                          struct OFBitmap *);

   FUNCTION
	Draws glyph as OF_RasterGlyph does, through matrix: four LONGs,
	16.16 pixels to the em, y up. A point (x, y) of the outline in font
	units lands at
	    X = (x * matrix[0] + y * matrix[1]) / units per em
	    Y = (x * matrix[2] + y * matrix[3]) / units per em
	pixels from the origin, so {size, 0, 0, size} (each << 16) is a
	size in pixels, a different matrix[0] stretches the glyph across,
	matrix[1] shears it and the four together rotate it. The face's own
	pixel size is not used or changed. bm_XAdvance is the advance's x
	through the matrix. Free the bitmap with OF_FreeBitmap.

	For engines that make their own transforms, such as bullet.library.
	Check lib_Revision 1 or later before calling it.

   RESULT
	error - 0, or OFERR_ARGUMENT for an entry beyond 1024 pixels to the
	        em either way, OFERR_RANGE for a glyph over 16384 pixels
	        either way, OFERR_FONT, OFERR_MEMORY.

openfont.library/OF_RescanFonts                 openfont.library/OF_RescanFonts

   NAME
	OF_RescanFonts -- rebuild the font index now (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_RescanFonts()
	D0

	LONG OF_RescanFonts(void);

   FUNCTION
	Reads every font folder again and saves the index, whether or not a
	folder's date changed. OF_FindFaceA does this by itself when one
	did; call this after changing a font in place. Must be called from
	a process.

openfont.library/OF_SetSize                         openfont.library/OF_SetSize

   NAME
	OF_SetSize -- set a face's pixel size (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = OF_SetSize(face, pixels)
	D0                 A0    D0

	LONG OF_SetSize(struct OFFace *, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	The size shaping, metrics and rasterising use from now on. A
	fallback takes the size of the face it serves when it shapes.

openfont.library/OF_ShapeA                           openfont.library/OF_ShapeA

   NAME
	OF_ShapeA -- shapes a run with a script, language, direction and features (V1, revision 3)
	OF_Shape -- varargs stub

   SYNOPSIS
	count = OF_ShapeA(face, text, length, glyphs, capacity, tags)
	D0                A0    A1    D0      A2      D1        A3

	ULONG OF_ShapeA(struct OFFace *, CONST_APTR, ULONG, struct OFGlyph *,
	                ULONG, const struct TagItem *);
	ULONG OF_Shape(struct OFFace *, CONST_APTR, ULONG, struct OFGlyph *,
	               ULONG, Tag, ...);

   FUNCTION
	Shapes the run [OFA_Offset, OFA_Offset + OFA_Length) of text, with
	the whole text as its context, as OF_ShapeText does, and more:

	- OFA_UTF16 TRUE: text is UTF-16 (UWORDs) and length, offsets,
	  feature ranges and gl_Cluster count 16-bit units. A surrogate pair
	  is one character; a lone surrogate is U+FFFD.
	- OFA_Script: the run's ISO 15924 code ('Arab', 'Hebr', 'Latn');
	  0 takes it from the text.
	- OFA_Language: the OpenType language system ('TRK ', 'SRB '), for
	  the font's own forms (locl); 0 the script's default.
	- OFA_Direction: OFDIR_LTR, OFDIR_RTL, or OFDIR_AUTO (from the
	  script). Right to left, mirrored characters take their mirrors
	  and the glyphs still come left to right: the run's last character
	  first.
	- OFA_Features, OFA_NumFeatures: struct OFFeature, each turning a
	  feature on (of_Value 1, or n for the n-th alternate) or off (0)
	  over a range of the text, or all of it.

	Arabic, Syriac, N'Ko, Mongolian and the other joining scripts join
	(isol, fina, medi, init), and Hebrew points and Arabic harakat are
	put in the order fonts expect. Fallbacks work as for OF_ShapeText.

   RESULT
	count - the glyphs the run has (up to capacity written); 0 on
	        failure. Call with glyphs NULL to measure.

openfont.library/OF_ShapeText                     openfont.library/OF_ShapeText

   NAME
	OF_ShapeText -- shape a run of text into glyphs (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	count = OF_ShapeText(face, utf8, bytes, glyphs, capacity)
	D0                   A0    A1    D0     A2      D1

	ULONG OF_ShapeText(struct OFFace *, CONST_STRPTR, ULONG,
	                   struct OFGlyph *, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	Shapes the text with OpenType's rules (ligatures, kerning, marks,
	the script's own), guessing its script and direction. Clusters the
	face has no glyphs for are shaped with its fallbacks, in order.
	Writes up to capacity glyphs, in visual order.

   INPUTS
	glyphs - may be NULL, to learn how many to allocate.

   RESULT
	count - how many glyphs the run has, even when more than capacity.
	        0 on failure.

openfont.library/OF_Version                         openfont.library/OF_Version

   NAME
	OF_Version -- OpenFont's own version (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	version = OF_Version()
	D0

	ULONG OF_Version(void);

   RESULT
	version - OpenFont's version (not the library's): major in the
	          upper word, minor in the lower.
